        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Marinelli Glacier, Alberto de Agostini National Park, Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego, South America, Strait of Magellan\n- Concepts: tidewater glacier, place names\n\nFacts:\n- Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego is an island near the southern tip of South America and is separated from the mainland by the Strait of Magellan.\n- Tierra del Fuego literally means \"Land of the Fire,\" was formerly called \"Isla de Xativa,\" and is also known as Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego.\n- Marinelli Glacier is a tidewater glacier located in Alberto de Agostini National Park on Isla Grande de Tierra del Fuego.",
